          and ws_sales_price / ws_list_price BETWEEN 53 * 0.01 AND 63 * 0.01\n                  ) or\n    exists (select *\n            from catalog_sales,date_dim, item\n            where c.c_customer_sk = cs_ship_customer_sk and\n                  cs_sold_date_sk = d_date_sk and\n                  d_year = 2001 and\n                  d_moy between 9 and 9+3 and\n                  cs_item_sk = i_item_sk and\n                  i_category in (\'Home\', \'Jewelry\', \'Shoes\')\n                  and i_manager_id BETWEEN 28 and 37\n                  and cs_sales_price / cs_list_price BETWEEN 53 * 0.01 AND 63 * 0.01\n                  ))\n group by cd_gender,\n          cd_marital_status,\n          cd_education_status,\n          cd_purchase_estimate,\n          cd_credit_rating,\n          cd_dep_count,\n          cd_dep_employed_count,\n          cd_dep_college_count\n order by cd_gender,\n          cd_marital_status,\n          cd_education_status,\n          cd_purchase_estimate,\n          cd_credit_rating,\n          cd_dep_count,\n          cd_dep_employed_count,\n          cd_dep_college_count\nlimit 100;\n```\n\nQuery Rewrite Strategies:\nQuery Rewrite 1:\n"""The matched case (Case 1) explains the SQL query changes as follows:\n\nThe original query had an outer projection layer that renamed the columns, but did not transform them. The rewrite rule eliminated this layer and directly applied the aggregate functions and `GROUP BY` to the original data source. This resulted in a more efficient query execution plan.\n\nIn summary, the query rewrite rule applied Case 1 of the rule to the given SQL query, eliminating the outer projection layer and directly applying the aggregate functions and `GROUP BY` to the original data source."""\n\nQuery Rewrite 2:\n"""The original query is slow because of the NOT EXISTS condition. The rewritten query uses a LEFT OUTER JOIN instead, which can be more efficient. This approach replaces the subquery with a join, which can reduce the number of rows being processed and improve performance."""\n...\n\nQuery Rewrite N: """..."""'}], 'response': "Here's a summary of the provided SQL query rewrite strategies in one paragraph:\n\nThe given SQL query can be rewritten using various strategies to optimize its execution. One approach is to eliminate an outer projection layer, directly applying aggregate functions and `GROUP BY` to the original data source, resulting in a more efficient query plan (Query Rewrite 1). Another strategy involves replacing a NOT EXISTS condition with a LEFT OUTER JOIN, which can reduce the number of rows being processed and improve performance (Query Rewrite 2).", 'time': 1.1977839469909668}
